  "schoolyard_use_notes": "This tree features glossy, dark green leaves that are thick and leathery, perfect for lessons on leaf structure and water retention. Its pink to mauve flowers bloom in clusters, offering a chance to explore pollination and flower anatomy. The tree produces woody seed capsules that can be used to discuss seed dispersal and plant reproduction. Its tolerance to coastal conditions makes it a good example for studies on plant adaptation to different environments.",
